      "id": 1,
      "text": "Patterson sprang up in 1846 when the Big Four Railroad cut through the forest, turning the village into a bustling lumber and grain hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/patterson_ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1848 Isaiah Ickes opened a tannery, and by 1863 a warehouse had been converted into a grist mill that fed the growing community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/patterson_ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Patterson Field was renamed in 1931, becoming part of the larger Wright‑Patterson Air Force Base that today hosts the 88th Air Base Wing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wright-Patterson_Air_Force_Base",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Along P Street in Patterson lie Adena culture mounds, prehistoric earthworks that once marked the territory of ancient Native American peoples.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wright-Patterson_Air_Force_Base",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 88th Air Base Wing, stationed at Wright‑Patterson, employs more than 5,000 officers, enlisted airmen, civilians and contractors who keep the base running.",
